    "broke-my-mug-not-my-song":{search:"I can hear the birds chirping and the sun\u2019s setting, but it\u2019s bright. Squinting my eyes in the light. It\u2019s a world full of people and sounds. My place in this is lost, never found, never settles down. I might be touching ground, have been flying with my life. Wonder if what I imagined will feel worth it when it\u2019s right. Suppose I\u2019ll still feel misery whether I stay close to ground, Or whether I lift off into galaxies unbound, and never come back down. And I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m healing, Or just learning how to float. I keep reaching for a feeling That I swear I used to know. Maybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud, Made to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds. Maybe I\u2019ll find peace where the stars don\u2019t make a sound, Or maybe I\u2019ll lift off and never come back down. Never come back down. Never come back down. If I can\u2019t find my place here, I\u2019ll be somewhere I can\u2019t be found. I can hear the world moving like it knows where it should go. Everybody\u2019s got a rhythm, I\u2019m just standing in the glow. Trying to look normal with a storm behind my eyes. Smiling at the sunset while I\u2019m disappearing inside. And maybe I\u2019m dramatic, maybe I just feel too much. Maybe I\u2019m just tired from surviving without touch. Maybe all this distance is the price of staying proud. Maybe I\u2019m already gone and just haven\u2019t said it loud. And I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m breaking, Or becoming something new. I keep staring at the sky Like it might tell me what to do. Maybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud, Made to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds. Maybe I\u2019ll find peace where the stars don\u2019t make a sound, Or maybe I\u2019ll lift off and never come back down. Never come back down. Never come back down. If I can\u2019t find my place here, I\u2019ll be somewhere I can\u2019t be found. Close to ground, I feel the weight. Far from home, I feel the same. Call it freedom, call it fate. Either way, I carry pain. But there\u2019s a light I haven\u2019t reached. There\u2019s a version I might meet. Maybe somewhere past this grief, There\u2019s a life that feels like me. Maybe I was made to run, made to rise, made to burn out loud, Made to chase the sun through the dark side of the clouds. Maybe I\u2019ll find peace where the stars don\u2019t make a sound, Or maybe I\u2019ll lift off and never come back down. Never come back down. Never come back down. If I can\u2019t find my place here, I\u2019ll be somewhere I can\u2019t be found. I can hear the birds chirping and the sun\u2019s setting, but it\u2019s bright. Squinting my eyes in the light. It\u2019s a world full of people and sounds. My place in this is lost, never found, never settles down. I woke up in a supermarket cathedral, Wearing a necktie made of caution tape. The moon was frying eggs on a car hood, And the sun had a raccoon for a face. I saw a preacher selling discount halos, Two for one beside the laundromat. A fish in a business suit kept screaming, \u201cYou can\u2019t die yet, you still owe me tax.\u201d Everything\u2019s sticky, everything\u2019s loud, There\u2019s a clown in the mirror eating thunderclouds. I\u2019d laugh if my teeth weren\u2019t glued to the floor, Knocking on heaven through a bathroom door. Needing connection does not make you weak, It makes you human, tragically. A gorgeous disaster with coffee-stain wings, Dragging a throne through a yard sale of kings. Needing connection does not make you weak, It makes you human, unfortunately. A shopping cart chariot, flat tire dreams, Still somehow rolling through the gasoline rain. There\u2019s a choir of pigeons in a casino, Singing hymns through a nicotine storm. A beauty queen vomits glitter in slow-mo, While Cupid gets arrested for fraud. The sky wears fishnets, the road smells jealous, There\u2019s a black-tie funeral for dignity. A mime got rich selling invisible sandwiches, Now he owns half the city and three minor seas. Everything\u2019s melting, everything bites, There\u2019s a priest on a skateboard blessing fistfights. I\u2019d pray if the ceiling would stop chewing gum, And the jukebox quit swallowing everyone. Needing connect",snippet:"I can hear the birds chirping and the sun\u2019s setting, but it\u2019s bright.",clipIds:["647f2c65-84d5-4c21-8d96-a9affb3a20f2", "21e0c5e2-888a-4d8e-a97a-4ff092b72819", "d8ab709d-ca66-4f34-bd79-fcdc288aa190", "17868bfa-0361-45b5-8e94-f222da19a3a0", "89a032ef-af2d-4de0-b3b2-52424cbe7aa3", "5e905328-7db3-4230-b17c-249f91872755"]},
