    "friction-the-what":{search:"Title: Friction Verse 1 You\u2019re asking in the dark again, Could I have woken up back then? Could I have cracked the code at twenty-two, Seen the sky the way I do? Was there a door I should\u2019ve found? Some sacred switch, some hidden sound? Or did the fire take its time To burn the boy and forge the mind? Pre-Chorus You didn\u2019t need a chemical. You needed pressure, real and physical. Steel is shaped when heat persists \u2014 Not when comfort coexists. Chorus You didn\u2019t need acid. You needed friction. Walls and weight and contradiction. The van. The fall. The loss of vision. The break that built your definition. No shortcut. No clean incision. Just collision after collision. You didn\u2019t need magic. You needed friction. Verse 2 The van at minus thirty nights, Breath like ghosts in frozen light. Power dying. Mind on edge. Standing on a narrow ledge. The collapse of who you were, Good or evil \u2014 blurred and blurred. Identity in civil war, Love at the door you couldn\u2019t hold before. Pre-Chorus You tried to script a higher role, Strategist heart, divided soul. But truth doesn\u2019t arrive on cue \u2014 It waits until it ruins you. Chorus You didn\u2019t need acid. You needed friction. Loss of status. Loss of fiction. The break. The doubt. The contradiction. The rebuild under demolition. No shortcut. No superstition. Just repetition, repetition. You didn\u2019t need magic. You needed friction. Bridge (spoken / stripped down) Are you grieving a missed shortcut? Or honoring the long road you cut? Because evolution doesn\u2019t knock. It kicks the door. And takes the lock. Final Chorus (bigger, anthemic) You didn\u2019t need acid. You needed friction. Cold and chaos as ignition. The van. The girl. The self-division. The long, relentless expedition. No clean path. No permission. Just survival turned to vision. You didn\u2019t need magic. You needed friction. Asking in the dark again Could I have woken up back then Could I have cracked the code at twenty-two Seen the sky the way I do Was there a door I should have found Some sacred switch, some hidden sound Or did the fire take its time to burn The boy and forge the mind You didn't need a chemical You needed pressure, real and physical Steel is shaped when he persists Not when comfort coexists You didn't need acid, you needed friction Walls and weight and contradiction The van, the fall, the loss of vision The break that built your definition No shortcut, no clean incision Just collision after collision You didn't need magic (oh-oh) You needed friction The van at minus thirty-nine Breath like ghost in frozen light Powdered ice on etched Standing on a narrow ledge The collapse of who you were The good or evil, blurred and blur Identity in civil war Love at the door you couldn't hold before You tried to script a higher role Strategist, heart divided soul But truth doesn't arrive on cue It waits until it ruins you You didn't need acid, you needed friction Loss of status, loss of fiction The break, the doubt, the contradiction The rebuild under demolition No shortcut, no superstition Just repetition, repetition You didn't need magic (oh-oh) You needed friction Are you grieving a missed shortcut Honoring the long road you cut Because evolution doesn't knock It kicks the door and takes the lock You didn't need acid, you needed friction Cold and chaos as ignition The van, the girl, the self-division The long relentless expedition No clean path, no permission Just survival turned to vision You didn't need magic (oh-oh) You needed friction (Instrumental)",snippet:"Title: Friction",clipIds:["c625d417-2eb0-4c83-ba85-fd34afaa9d55", "b7ac1dad-0544-4cae-b1e8-08df43a16282", "5172d8f8-e641-4001-8655-cba27650a1f0"]},
