    "september-26th-heartbreak":{search:"I was gonna write a love song But, before it finished, she was long gone Gave her in my heart, watched her captivate it Then her s seat's vacant, she escaped quick I don't know if I could go Back to who I was, she touched my soul, I felt my heart flutter and my brain fuzz I asked myself if I could be Respectful of her time I took time to think of her as family This was the girl who sat two seats in front of me She set my heart wild and free Oh, I'm wild and free Whether or not I mean to be Yeah, I'm wild and free But my heart's unhappy 'Cause I wanna love I wanna feel I wanna hurt It's a packaged deal I wanna hurt 'cause I wanna feel 'cause I wanna love I'm choosing love Heartbreak, heartbreak I never knew what it'd be like to lose you Heartbreak, heartbreak Now I see It's a painful reality Heartbreak, heartbreak Comes and goes It makes us grow Heartbreak, heartbreak You water me You are a planter I am your seed I am your seed Growing wild and free I was gonna write a sad song But then another girl came along And was helping me with heart break and anxiety She's an INFJ, such a gentle pea I've got a tattoo of the Grim Reaper Oh, I'm wild and free Oh, I'm wild and free So, I'm gonna love I'm gonna feel I'm gonna hurt It's a package deal I'm gonna hurt 'cause I'm gonna feel 'cause I'm gonna love",snippet:"I was gonna write a love song",clipIds:["dff144e6-7de2-4ca0-af21-897de1a4da8d"]},
    "seven-days-locked":{search:"Seven days locked where the lights don\u2019t fade, Saw a man preaching fire like he carried the blade. He said angels were screaming through the hospital vents, I just smiled, played it cool, like I knew what he meant. If I lose my calm, then the room might break, But if I hold it steady, they\u2019ll all feel safe. I\u2019m the guard dog hiding in a paper gown, Growling quiet so no one drowns. I\u2019ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd, Carrying the weight, never saying it out loud. If the voices come knocking, I\u2019ll answer with grace, \u2019Cause somebody\u2019s gotta hold the space. He said God was a pilot and the floor was the sky, Tried to jump off his bed just to learn how to fly. I caught his arm, laughed, said \u201csave that trick, The food here\u2019s bad but the gravity\u2019s thick.\u201d If I lose my calm, then the room might break, But if I hold it steady, they\u2019ll all feel safe. I\u2019m the guard dog hiding in a paper gown, Growling quiet so no one drowns. I\u2019ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd, Carrying the weight, never saying it out loud. If the voices come knocking, I\u2019ll answer with grace, \u2019Cause somebody\u2019s gotta hold the space. Funny thing about hell\u2014sometimes it\u2019s just Tuesday, With bingo cards, pills, and the nurses on relay. But I learned in the storm when the world\u2019s insane, You can still be the calm in somebody else\u2019s brain. I\u2019ve been vicious with myself but a shield for the crowd, Carrying the weight, never saying it out loud. If the voices come knocking, I\u2019ll answer with grace, \u2019Cause somebody\u2019s gotta hold the space. Yeah\u2014somebody\u2019s gotta hold the space.",snippet:"Seven days locked where the lights don\u2019t fade,",clipIds:["3a9418e6-b884-413e-9135-d904e8bfde29", "278dbbac-3ada-456e-a44c-92eb3378be05", "509147ff-abdc-445c-a475-6548fa10cde3"]},
