    "where-monsters-are":{search:"A wandering monster escapes the jeers of the world And finds a ruined keep at the edge of the wild The maiden who tends to these broken, cursed halls Has spent years guarding legends that others reviled As he stalks through the shadows, he slowly can see That the castle reflects all the scars in her soul Quiet, and tender, with secrets and spells Hidden chambers and relics that never grow old While others feared her magic, or worshiped her grace They only touched the surface, then turned and were gone But he sees the aching beneath every smile And the beauty in battles she\u2019s fought for so long By the torchlight they share All their monsters and prayers Ancient runes start to glow in the stone Through the cracks in the walls Something living now calls Like the castle itself wants them home What began as a whisper in the cold, haunted air Grows into the first time they both feel seen there As the dark fades to dawn and the curses grow thin She unbinds the wild powers she hides from the rest Shows the claws in her kindness, the storms in her veins And the thorns in the gardens she guards in her chest He swears he is not just a traveler who strays Not another wide-eyed pilgrim who\u2019s eager, then leaves He lays down his armor, his teeth, and his rage And she slowly believes what his trembling heart weaves By the torchlight they share All their monsters and prayers Ancient runes start to glow in the stone Through the cracks in the walls Something living now calls Like the castle itself wants them home Love is not some bright spell in a ballroom of light It\u2019s the promise to stay through the howl of the night In the growl and the grace In the scars on each face They find mercy in all that they feared Not in crowns, not in gold But in stories retold Every chapter they hold as they draw near By the torchlight they stay Through the beast and the fray In the castle that once stood alone In the rage, in the rain In the monster and maiden They discover a heart made of stone Turning warm as they learn every wound, every scar That the wildest of love lives where monsters are",snippet:"A wandering monster escapes the jeers of the world",clipIds:["b36296ae-d623-41be-9174-30374fce081c", "9fc80b65-52ce-4930-b7f2-e61c4402a27b", "7bc7f95c-c813-4af9-bbf3-5ddf893afa85"]},
